> > In the vger tree, the default is to include both FBCON_CFB{8,32}.
> 
> Yes, that's all my patch to 2.1.113 did as well...
> 
> > Or are you talking about the TGA specific parts? These could easily depend 
> > on FBCON_HAS_CFB{8,32}, too.
> 
> The TGA code already does, somewhat; do you mean modifying the code so that
> more gets left out if you only select 8-plane support? I'm not sure it would
> be worth it... ???

Yes, that's what I mean. It doesn't make much sense to support e.g. 24 bit
boards if you have no support for 24 bit text consoles. Unless X is your
primary target.

> > In 8 bpp, it looks fine (without beer :-(.
> 
> Huh? I saw beer in both 8 and 32 bpp renderings; it made me thirsty... ;-}

Jakub Jelinek removed it from the vger tree after the big
Penguin/beer/nazy/cannabis/gay/catholic flamewar on linux-kernel.

> > > Sounds like a patch for Geert.  Hmm... if we use the 24-plane TGA
> > > code just a DIRECTCOLOR device the palette setup code could be
> > > thrown away.  Do any programs actually use the palette routines
> > > of the console?
> > 
> > It's the other way around: DIRECTCOLOR uses a palette, TRUECOLOR doesn't
> > (xc/doc/specs/Xserver/ddx.tbl.ms).
> 
> That's what I thought, too, but the code had it backwards, and I took the
> easy way out, setting what would get the correct rendering... ;-}
> 
> > Yes, the original frame buffer code was wrong w.r.t. this.
> 
