On Sat, Aug 08, 1998 at 01:20:46PM -0700, Richard Henderson wrote:
> Much nicer is to create temp files and to map them.  This
> also has the advantage of being pagable, and not having limits
> on the number or size of the mappings.

exactly that's what cdrecord doesn't want. To avoid dropouts during
burning, it creates a big fifo in memory. If parts of the fifo
gets swapped out and must be paged in, the fifo is worthless.

Thomas.

