Sigh; yes, MILO doesn't quite know how to handle a VGA behind a bridge; it
requires some special bridge setup that we're not doing right, yet.

On most boxes this isn't a problem - there are no slots behind a bridge
to put a VGA into, but on UX, MIATA, and NORITAKE family, there are... :-\

> 1) ldmilo.exe is unable to boot direct from a CD-ROM 

Does linload.exe?

> 2) milo.ful (I've not tried all milo.ful's arround) doesn't boot
>    large kernels.

Known problem: UX MILOs are not built with the same memory layout as the
MILOs for other platforms. Older MILOs would have had the same problems,
but we fixed this problem in them long enough ago so that you're not
remembering... ;-}

Note that the memory layout is forced upon the UX MILO by ldmilo.exe; the
MILO image itself is not loaded high enough in memory to be beyond the area
into which a large kernel image will unpack... :-\

> 3) I've never seen 2.1.xxx running on Ruffian. Same config (except 
>    CONFIG_ALPHA_SYSTYPE) works fine here on SX an LX boards.

I have patches for 2.1.113 that seem to run pretty well; they are part of
the patch set that contains generic kernel support that Richard and I are
working on.  I'll be sending these off to Richard quite soon, later today,
hopefully...

--Jay++

