OK, for the first hard drive ( root) put jumpers across:
7 and 8 - SCSI ID #1
A01 to A02 - term power supplied to bus
nothing else to play with on that one.

For the second hard disk jumper:
5 and 6 - SCSI ID #2
13 and 14 - enable termination.
A01 to A02 - term power supplied to bus
Put this drive at the end of the 68 line cable, farthest away from the SCSI
controller.


For the CDROM set it to ID #4.
termination enabled.

Now, if you use a 50 pin cable to the CDROM, and a 68 pin to the hard
drives as you described, you have the CDROM on an 8 bit bus on one side of
the card, and the HDs on a 16 bit bus on the other. This means that the
termination on the high 8 bit part of the 16 bit bus must be enabled on the
card. On the Fireport40 this is automatic, so no worries here.

If you can, it might be nice to pick up an active terminator to plug in at
the end of the 68 pin bus after the last hard drive, and turn off the
termination on the last HD. This is more stable. However, it might be
unnecessary..


Cheers,

