On Tue, 11 Aug 1998, Jeff Sturm wrote:
> On Tue, 11 Aug 1998, dca2 wrote:
> > I have decided to go with SCSI instead of IDE.  I have not used SCSI
> > before.. I wanted the 2940UW but settled for a Diamond Fireport 40. I
> > also picked up (2) - 1G IBM hard drives without documentation. Any one
> > with knowleged as to where to find info would be appreciated. I am
> > searching IBM now.
> > 
> > Also, I got some conflicting statements today about SCSI configuration.
> > The manual tells me to set boot drive to ID 0. The guy at the computer
> > store said the higher the number the higher the priority. What is best
> > the best solution? I still have to figure out how these are jumpered
> > too.
> 
> When two SCSI devices request the bus at the same time, the higher 
> numbered device always wins.  Normally the host adapter has the highest, 
> which is OK since it may frequently need to preempt the bus anyway.
> Disks are usually numbered starting at id 0.  I don't know a reason to do 
> it any other way.

I have the disk at 5 (used to be 6), CD-ROM at 3 and DAT at 4. So the disk has
a higher priority than the slow devices.

The disadvantage is the numbering of devices in Linux. Once I connected a Syjet
from a friend, and I had to move my disk from 6 to 5 to keep it sda, while the
Syjest was sdb (at 6).

Greetings,

