Piece of cake:
	Go to troll (ftp.troll.no? Somebody correct me if that's wrong)
and get QT1.33 (don't get 1.40 it does compile, but it will not run). I
would suggest getting the sources, and "rolling your own". easy to do,
and eliminates compatibility problems. 
	After that is installed, go to kde (ftp.kde.org) and get the
version 1 release (feeling brave? Try the snapshots, but only if you're
willing to put up with alpha code (no not DEC Alpha, new version alpha.
This stuff may or may not even compile, but it's the latest, and
greatest). So anyway, again, get the sources, and compile them. I've
heard WAY to many horror stories of strange behavior from trying to use
the pre-compiled stuff.
	Once you've rebuild the sources (there's directions at the web
site), you'll be rolling! I have it running on my Alpha, and it does
just fine. All of the release version sources built without intervention
on the first try!

	Go forth, and try... The worst that can happen is that you might
learn something.

