As far as partitions go.  Of course it be nice if each operating system
has their own hard drive (windows especially is very unfriendly) however
you can use different partitions.  Remember thought that Linux WILL see
DOS but does will not see Linux.  As far as DOS is concern Linux doesn't
exist, partitions that linux is under don't exist. Nothing exist but
Microsoft... ahhh sorry got carried away there <G>  In other words when
you partition your drive in lets say 4 ways and put linux on 3 when you
go into windows all you are going to see is drive "C" and nothing else.

It is a good idea to have at least 4 partitions one (small) for DOS FAT
that way both NT and Linux loader can exist there, another one for
windows then last two for Linux (one of those for swap)

Hope this helps
Marek

