Check Microway. There's another one but I think it's
more like f2c from another company. Only other real FORTRAN
compiler I know of is Microway's. It's only 32 bit
though, last I heard. Also, I second the
comment on libffm. (free fast math) If you use lots
of basic functions like cos/sin/exp/sqrt, etc.

If performance is critical, buy DEC UNIX/FORTRAN.
It's an additional $3500 or so per box. Also,
consider profiling your code to see what the real
HOG is and fix it...


Wes


