Hello!

> With regards to your message at 07:13 PM 08-13-98 -0500, Artimage. Where
> you stated:
> >Has anyone actually done video capturing on an Alpha? I've seen some intel
> >frame grabbers, but I haven't seen anything that led me to believe there
> >is an alpha port. Any help? 
> A friend has done it on a card with a Brooktree RAMDAC. I believe the
> BT885, off the top of my memory..
The Brooktree chip is no RAMDAC. It's a full PCI bus master capapable frame
grabber device copying the digitized video frames directly into the video
memory of your graphics card.
The chip is named bt848 and is available on many cards, beginning with the
well known Hauppauge WinTV. It is also available on a more primitive card
without HF tuner and VideoText for less money (about $50 max.).

> There are quite a few cards with this same chip..
Right. And it works even with Alphas ;)

