According to Randy Carpenter:
> 
> 
> Can someone tell me where to get a *working* rpm for redhat 5.0 alpha for
> an xntp server?  I have trid some of the rpm's in the redhat contrib, but
> all give me errors, and the latest srpm is would not insall correctly...
> 
> Once i have a proper rpm installed, can anyone point me to some info on
> how to set up xntp as a server.  I don't need it to be a client, but a
> server.
> 

I'm not sure what you mean by "working" -- if you mean that the clocks
won't sync, you will need to apply a 1 line patch to line 53 of
/usr/src/linux/kernel/sched.c:

-int tickadj = 500/HZ;
+int tickadj = 500/HZ ? : 1;

If you mean by not working that ntpdate generates tons of error messages
about poll, then you need the recent updates to (if memory serves) glibc
and the kernel.  I'm running glibc-2.0.7-19 and kernel-2.0.35-1 (-2 includes
the 1 line patch above).

And if you mean something else, file a bug report and it will be fixed :-)

73 de Jeff

