>I'll change cables and try it. The cable I am using is used. I do have a
>new cable that came with adapter card.
No, the bus number is 0, the SCSI ID of the controller is 7.
Here it is in full syntax:
Bus 0, ID 7, LUN 0.

If you were to install a second SCSI card that would be:
Bus 1, ID 7, LUN 0

devices on the bus are as follows:
Hard drive at ID0, first SCSI card:
Bus 0, ID 0, LUN 0

And its partitions:
Bus 0, ID 0, LUN 0, part 1
Bus 0, ID 0, LUN 0, part 2
Or in Linux talk:
/dev/sda1
/dev/sda2

