>One question that popped into my mind was the cable. Are 3 or more connector
>cables directional? Or can I install them to suit the box? There is a longer
>distance between beginning and first connector than other end and connector.

SCSI cables are just a bunch of wires. They aren't directional. They ARE
handed, so don't put them in the sockets backwards. On the other hand they
are usually keyed. Or , to put it another way, the edge with the strip goes
closest to the power connector.

>Secondly. On my 50 pin CDRom I am going to use the supplied cable. It has 4
>connectors. I will use the end and one more. Should I use the end connector?
>the first connector? And again, direction, I am going to guess that the
>largest distance between connectors is the card end?

Don't have a cable hanging past the last device, UNLESS you put a
terminator on the end of that cable..

>Lastly, I may be reading the CDRom label wrong...where it points to the
>terminator jumper it says:

>"Termination-short off"  I am reading this to mean no jumper is terminated.

