Great! The AS1000 (Mikasa) is a great machine. You can boot off either
via SRM or ARC (2 bioses, how's that for flexibility!)...

Most experienced Alpha users prefer SRM because it's commandline and
more flexible....newbies prefer ARC because it's menu-driven and hence
easier but eventually migrate to SRM.

Alphas require diskettes, because the regular "bootable" CDROMs are
bootable only by Intel CPUs... I haven't tried the RH5.1 Alpha CDs yet
(anyone tried to boot off a RH5.1 Alpha CD?).

As usual RTFM:

The Alpha/Linux Homepage:
