If you can't feel anything in your hd then there is a good chance that
they are not working.  You could check to make sure that they don't have
a jumper setting that will take a power away from a drive, but an older
driver like that I don't believe you would have a problem with that.  As
far as your floppy is concern I would make sure that you didn't connect
cable the wrong way.  You have to make sure that the end of a cable with
twisted wire in the middle goes to the floppy (and the red stripe on
your cable goes towards the power supply).  Also you have to make sure
that the other end of a cable is plugged into the motherboard with the
stripe end facing the pin # 1 (usually you can just look for a little 1
by the floppy connector).  Hopefully that will help you in upgrading the
firmware, if not try to use different floppy.

As far as your CD-ROM is concern... I don't remember did you say you
tried different cable?

Take care
Marek

