> Where can one find ways to put milo in flash?  Is there a way I can
Ouh ... I had to search a long time before I finally came up with something
like fmu.gz? Or something very obviously like this. This is a bootable MILO
image that contains the flash program. Look at the MILO archive on Digital's
FTP site.

> recover my flash if I ever decide to use arc again?  I don't want this
> Loader loading a loader which loads a loader which boots the machine!
 ;) That's the BSD does it :)) The first time I wanted to install BSD on a
DECstation the HowTo said: First you will need a helper machine with BSD
already installed. For the installation of the helper machine I would need a
helper machine which would ... you think the rest.
OK. But MILO can indeed boot those firmware installation floppies from
Digital and can so be exchanged with whatever flashable bootloader you want.
