> Here is where I screwed up.  I went through the above procedure again, but
> installed MILO at block zero.  Unfortunately I didn't realize that that was
> where the failsafe loader lived.  I did get MILO installed, though.
> 

Restoring the failsafe loader is not easy.  I've done it on the PC164 and
it's even more complicated on the LX164.  The procedure requires using
the SROM mini-debugger but the standard LX164 SROM does not include the
mini-debugger.  A special debug SROM must be used which has the memory 
hard configured at 64MB.  

I don't know where you can get an LX164 debug SROM.  You might have to
get an Evaluation Board Software Development Kit (EBSDK) CD, version 2.2
or above, and try to make your own. 

good luck,

