This is a clever hack. Another way to get this, more conventional, is
to use RedHat's JumpStart, which is available from 5.0 on. A third way
is to hack up an install disk to ask one question and then dd its
entire drive over the network; that's how I did mine. Each one is a
little different.

With Bruce's technique, you need to get all your slaves' hardware
ethernet addresses into the bootp server, which is kind of
annoying. With RedHat's jumpstart, you have to do the same. Mine's
kind of hacky and isn't for the faint of stomach.

