Which partition are you trying to write the tar file to?

If that parition is NFS mounted to the Intel, it won't work, but on a
local file system it shouldn't be a problem (assuming tar isn't
broken).

The attached program creates a 3GB sparse file on a local filesystem
(I just made this quick test now and don't have enough disk space
free for a real file).

If it doesn't work, please send me the output of strace over it or
echo $? after it terminates.


