Hi Armin !

> 1. I cannot mount or read the CDROM from any Windows or Linux box
>    The University dude told me the CDROM has a ufs Filesystem. really?

You can. It is ufs and if you compile ufs support in your kernel
you can mount it. (I've tried it only on development kernels and
it worked fine.)

> 2. All my PCI Cards seem to be pretty useless with DU
>    The 2940 SCSI, the 3com 905 and the S3Virge cards do not work in SRM or
>    DU. What cards would you recommend as a replacemant for DU and Linux ?

Tulip-based network-card work fine.
NCR-based (53c8xx) cards are supported.
Some Mach64-based cards and TGA cards work.
 
> 3. The University dude told me i would need a DEC CDrom drive in order to
>    install it. Is that true, do i really need a DEC SCSI Drive, or can i
>    install it from any SCSI CDrom Drive ?

Not from any. Normally, a CD-ROM uses 2048 bytes/sect and DU wants 1024b/s or
512b/s. Some drives support this modes and some do not.
It's worth to try.

