On Tue, 18 Aug 1998, Stefan Reinauer wrote:
> I've been playing around with AXP framebuffer support and I did not
> succeed in getting 2.1.115 booted with vgafb enabled.
> (machine hangs after printing the kernel version)
> I have an LX164 board and a Diamond FireGL 1000Pro (PermediaII) gfx
> adapter.
> 
> Some questions..
> 
> * Is this supposed to work on AXP Linux at all?

It's reported not to work on PPC neither :-( Probably a small adressing
difference that doesn't matter on Intel. Vgacon and vgafb are similar, they're
both VGA text mode drivers and originated from the same code.

> * Shouldn't I see the nice tux logo at bootup?

No. Only on graphical consoles.

> * Is the fact that vgafb only supports textmode a lack of an implementor 
>   or isn't it possible to implement such a thing.

It's more difficult to write a graphical frame buffer device for plain VGA due
to the banking issues. Vgafb was a quick hack to support VGA text mode within
the frame buffer devices paradigm.

But you're better off using vgacon. It'll perform better (faster scrolling).
And now you can start with vgacon and switch over to frame buffer devices
later, vgafb is really obsolete.

> * Why isn't it possible to use the atyfb on x86 or AXP Platforms? There
>   are many pci cards with a mach64 chipset out there.

Because no one tried? Atyfb now has PCI probing (was added for UltraSPARC), so
it may work on AXP and ia32. Feel free to try.

Greetings,

						Geert

