Wes Bauske wrote:
> 
> It surprises me that tar has the problem because the same
> problem would exist on Cray's and under DEC UNIX so it should
> have been sorted out a while back.

I do not remember ever seeing problems with GNU tar on Digital Unix
machines and I used it to write to a tape pretty sizeable file
systems.  Therefore I sugested that maybe a problem is somewhere
in VFS layer; but I have no idea what exactly it is.

cpio is not using the same format as tar.  GNU cpio indeed can read
tapes written with tar.

I suggested afio as well as it can compress stored files on file-by-file
basis so maybe one can bypass your problem (for a short while).
You will need to compile afio on your AIX system if you want to read
these tapes there.  AIX restore may be able to read tapes produced
by dump; you will have to try.

AFAIK pax is POSIXed version of tar; it does not seem to be very popular
as it is pretty restrictive and inherits deficiences of tar.

  Michal


