I think you'll have much better luck with the MILO and stuff on the RUFFIAN
floppy image file on gatekeeper.dec.com:

	/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/Test-Milos-2.0.30+/ruffian.img

Also, the RUFFIAN kernel on RH 5.1 ought to be fine; and you should be able
to work with the stock RH 5.1 RAMdisk, ie you don't need the Deskstation one,
and besides, it's from 4.2 IIRC... ;-}

If you wish to boot MILO from harddisk, be aware that you'll need to
format the MILO partition using other than LINUX's mkdosfs, as the RUFFIAN
console does not currently like the format. I've successfully used the
arcinst.exe that appears in \alpha on the NT 4.0 CD.

Good luck.

