Larry Creech wrote:
> 
> Why does my Pentium MMX compile a kernel twice as fast as the the Alpha? 

One of the most obvious reasons that it compiles totally different code,
using not exactly the same compiler, for a processor with registers
and opcodes half of a width of those on your Alpha.  Also optimizing
for RISC is much more costly than doing that for CISC.

In summary: "apples and oranges"  (and this does not even tries to
go into various differences in your hardware; raw processor cycle
count does not say very much).

  --mj


