64MB SIMMs  ARE expensive. Being Single Inline Memory Modules, the
chipcount has to stay low, dictating very large ( and expensive) chips.

Also, being fairly uncommon, they do not benefit from economy of scale.

I looked up the parts for you:
16M36, ECC SIMM, 72 pin, tin lead, 60ns: $197 each. Yup, they're not cheap.


