Depends which board he has.
If it is the PC164-500MHz, he has to use banks of 4, and banks of 8 are
better, as this then supports a 128 bit memory path.

It it is an older board, such as Cabriolet (EB64 or PCI64) you also have to
go 4 at a time.

Nonames would take pairs, but why spend this much on a noname?  ;^}


