I just built a linux 2.0.34 kernel under redhat on my Alpha PC164, and
was thinking of using it as an internet gateway for my Wearable Wireless
Webcam (http://wearcam.org).

I was wondering if anyone has used axattach on the DEC Alpha.

Alternatively, has anyone used slattach?  If so, where did you obtain DEC
Alpha versions of axattach and slattach?

I also experimented with PLIP (since there's nothing like plattach or the
like needed).

However, I find when I run PLIP (insmod plip, ifconfig... route...), sometimes
the computer "hangs" (doesn't respond to keypresses and cursor is frozen on
screen).

Thus I am wondering if anyone has had reliabile PLIP, and SLIP connections on a
PC164, or if it would make more sense for me to continue using a P.C. i386
architecture for a gateway (perhaps using ipfwadm to route packets over to
the DEC Alpha).


Best regards,


Steve Mann,
University of Toronto
http://wearcomp.org


