>Uhmmm, where can I get kernel-2.0.35-1 or kernel-2.0.35-2 ?  They are
not
>on Red Hat's ftp site.   I installed the glibc updates, and still get
>errors when running xntp.

I got mine from /pub/rehdat/updates/5.1/alpha, on the uk sunsite mirror
(src.doc.ic.ac.uk/Mirrors/ftp.redhat.com). there's only 2.0.25-1 there,
which
i presume is all that's currently available. Runs fine on a samsung
lx164/600MHz
box, although i *still* seem to be getting memory leakage, but i suspect
that's
a hardware problem.

>On a different note, does anyone knwo why on my alpha (533sx) the time
>would get reset to 1942, in the EWT timezone?  Along these same lines,
it
>takes 30 seconds or so to read the hardware clock

I got the same problem on the above box, except I got Jun 30 BDST 1942
(what
the **** is BDST BTW?). This was due to the fact that i had the
following set in
/etc/sysconfig/clock:
CLOCKMODE=ARC
ARC=true
UTC=false
 However, I was actually booting via SRM, so it was just reading some
total garbage
from a particular memory address to get the 1942 date. I found setting
clockmode 
to UTC fixed the problem. Then I found that the date set in SRM was 24
hours behind...
I you're actually booting via ARC then i can only presume we've found
some weird & 
wonderful bug. Either that or mickeysoft have started programming the
alpha firmware....

cheers,
john


