> How do I up the inodes/fd's ?

This is apparently a long-standing kernel bug, and RedHat and the
typical alpha kernel hackers all apparently don't have an example
system which displays the bug.

cat 8192 > /proc/sys/kernel/file-max
cat 8192 > /proc/sys/kernel/inode-max

But this just delays the problem. If you look around proc and count
the number of fd's actually opened by programs. You could also strace
syslogd etc to find out what errors it is actually getting.

-- g


