The KDE file manager does do a credible job of browsing (although it
won't do java or handle things like password authentication).

I'd be careful of compiled binaries of KDE though, there are a lot of
different versions for various Alpha releases and you can get into
trouble for example if you use QT libs that were compiled with gcc and
KDE binaries that were compiled with egcs. IMHO you are far better off
compiling KDE yourself, it's really not that hard.

