I doubt it is possible to get a perfect emulator for at least two reasons:

1. If you only have the binary it is sometimes difficult to impossible
   to differentiate between code and data. There is no garantee that 
   there is only code in text segments and data in data segments.
   Even some compilers seem to mix it.
2. Self modifing code is not too popular at the moment, but at
   asm level you can do very funny things. At least blow emulators.

> What we need is to support Java. We need Sparc, Alpha, PPC and Intel guys
> to demand for Java-based apps. Java will perform well for office-suite
> type software, and loads of other apps. For something like CAD, you 

I thinks the same. For all these apps that are 70+ % GUI Java is ideal.
And with JIT Compilers or Bytecode to nativecompilers the performance
hit is insignificant.

Java bytecode is nothing more than the machinelanguage of a 
software cpu. All you need is an emulator for it ;-)

thorsten

