On Sat, Aug 22, 1998 at 04:26:20PM -0400, José Pedro Sousa do Amaral wrote:
> I am yet another member of the Onsale club and am still assembling my 
> system. Can the AS 200 4/233 operate a fast wide SCSI-2 hard disk or is 
> it limited to SCSI-2 only hard disks?

I tried to install an Adaptec 3940W controller (dual wide), and had
mixed success.  SRM firmware doesn't see it.  Booting the kernel over
the network, Linux found the 3940W and attached IBM DHFS wide drive,
and *seemed* to work fine.  But I could not boot from it.  The kernel
would die instantly.  It's beyond me why it worked as a secondary disk
but not the primary.

You might have better luck with an NCR wide controller or a Qlogic
controller.  The NCR controller on the motherboard is narrow.  If your
wide drive can work on a narrow bus (with a cable adapter), things might
be fine.  I have such an adapter for my IBM drive, but I haven't had
much luck with it.  I lose every other byte on transfers returned from
the drive...  I haven't tried it on the AS200 yet -- But that's what
happened on a BusLogic controller.

Good luck,

Jeff


