> >>> "Dr P. Caleb Dhanasekaran" said:
> > 
> > I am trying to install RedHat linux 5.1 on my newly
> > bought AlphaPC 164UX/BX, 4MB cache, 21164A 600MHz processor
> > with IBM  Ultrastar ES 4.5 G UW SCSI hard disk.
> 
> If you wish to boot MILO from harddisk, be aware that you'll need to
> format the MILO partition using other than LINUX's mkdosfs, as the RUFFIAN
> console does not currently like the format. I've successfully used the
> arcinst.exe that appears in \alpha on the NT 4.0 CD.

I believe the ARC convention is that the "system partition" (where OS
bootstraps like MILO live) is type 6 (DOS 16-bit >=32 MB), and the
partition is formatted as 16-bit (not 12-bit) FAT.  I think that for
small partitions, mkdosfs defaults to 12-bit FAT, and you have to
override it on the command line.

I don't have a 164UX/BX to try this on, but it worked on my XL 300 with
AlphaBIOS.

