This is not a problem for AS200 but, personal preferences aside,
we have now boards for which SRM simply does not exist (boooo!).
DHCP option is also not present for the current UX. :-(

The other deficiency of SRM is lack of a provision for booting
multiple OSes from the same disk.  You have one boot block and that
is about it.  Or I am missing something here?

> It would also be possible to use the "MILO-flash technology" for a
> NELO (network-loader) under ARC ;-} 

With this small fly in the ointment that flashed MILO (or a mythical NELO)
may not perform all initializations properly.  This works on some boards,
like Cabriolet, but for others it may, or may not, work.  Jay posted
a number of times explaining why this is the case.  In short, MILO does
depend on ARC.

  Michal


