I have been experimenting with firewall tool kit on Linux.  I work with
nothing but Gauntlet all day, and very nicely configured tool kits, and I
thought it would be a challenge to get the took kit working on Linux.  I
did get it all up in x86 Linux, and my next step was to go and see if I
could configure the same thing to work on the Alpha system I have.  I got
it all up and working, the only problems I really had were to get the BSD
versions of libskey ported to Linux.

The goal of using fwtk on my alpha system was to use Skey Authentication
via login-sh and authsrv.  The way it works is just awesome, and adds a
huge step of security into your box.  I have a x86 Linux box acting as the
server, and the Alpha connects to it as a client for authentication.  Its
very impressive to see that working.  

Another nice thing is you can use Crypto Cards, and Secure ID cards with
this too.  Its all a matter of compiling the support into authsrv.

I just thought someone on this list might find that intersting, if you want
to know more email me and I will be glad to help you out.

