I just got an application to work on both Linux and NT on an Alpha.

My machine is a Microway screamer (21164) at 600MHZ.  The Linux compiler
is egcs-1.0.3a-1.  The NT compiler is MS Visual C++.

The application uses a lot of single precision floating point math.

Time in seconds:

Linux:  2.83
Linux with libffm: 2.63
NT: 2.47

PentiumII at 400MHZ under NT: 3.5 (Haven't tested a Linux version on PII)

I guess one way of looking this is that Linux has an Alpha compiler that is
nearly as good as Microsoft's.  Another way is that there is probably a
lot of improvement possible in the Linux compiler since I doubt that the
Microsoft compiler is that good on the Alpha.

Any comments?

Jon


