From: Joe Reiter <JReiter@truelink.com> Mon, 24 Aug 1998

> On my Multia, I cannot get it to talk to modems correctly.

My UDB talks to a USR Sportster 9600 on the 2nd port. I made the
Y cable using the following connections:
Modem  UDB
2      14
3      16
4      19  <- not used by modem
5      13  <- not used by modem
6      23
7      7   <- shared with port 1
8      12
20     11
You could also connect 22 to 22, but I didn't have enough wires.

I use kermit because I found minicom setup too flakey and unreliable,
but that could just be ignorance on my part.

I wired Port A for a terminal as follows:
Terminal  UDB
2         3
3         2
4         5
5         4
6         20  <- not used by terminal
7         7
8         8  <- not used by terminal
20        6  <- not used by terminal

Hope that helps,
Larry Z.

