Hello,

i've reading this list for a while and i will
collect some problems and solutions with the
ALPHA Motherboard 164SX with 21164PC CPU.

Please send questions, problems and of course 
solutions to me direct. I will post it to the
list.

OK, let's start ..

Hardware:
--------

MB: 	ALPHA Motherboard 164SX
CPU:	21164PC CPU 533 MHz.
FD:	3 1/2
HD: 	Seagate IDE
CDROM: 	ASUS 34x IDE

System:
------

RedHat 5.1

1. Install Problems with boot and kernel floppy from
   RH CDROM. Read Error on floppy drive.

--> DMA controller aren't initialized in kernel since
    2.0.30. USE DMA-Patch. 

2. Unexpected Interrupts after booting kernel and touch
   ide controller and UART. 

--> No solution at the moment.

3. HD-LED don't light with seagate drive on first IDE
   channel. Quantum drive seems ok.

--> Looks like the seagate drive aren't conform with 
    their AT-Interface. Well with other controllers
    the drive works very well. 
    No really a problem. We must use the LED connector
    from drive direct and connect it to the HD LED on
    the MB with some kind of logic. 

4.  Clock Problem on SX boards. The clock runs to slow
    or sometimes to fast.

--> This seems no problem any more in kernel 2.0.35.

5.  Auto-power-off don't use with 164SX.

--> Well, any ideas?

08/25/98

Some features i miss:
--------------------

1.  IDE controller use only PIO mode 0 or 1 (240ns)

Is anybody working at this??
It's simple to add some code to bios32.c to setup
the ide on the cy82c693 to PIO mode 4 or maybe
BUS Master DMA. 

BUS MASTER IDE: Who's working at it?

2. Parallel port should be initialized to ECP spp (mode0)
   if found. Maybe this is better done in drivers/
   So lptune should be enhanced.

3. APM not work for alpha (is it correct?)

   The cy82c693 and the smc super i/o controller
   have full support of power down modes with different
   events and timers. We should use this.



