I have PCMCIA support working on my 200 4/233 running rh 5.1. I used the 
pcmcia-cs.3.0.4 source with the alpha patch on a 2.0.34 kernel.  Follow
all the directions in the pcmcia-howto and it should work fine.  I ran
into
one problem, when the i82365.o module was loaded, it wanted to use an
IRQ
that something else was using (maybe the scsi controller), and caused
the
system to lock up.  As the pcmcia package automatically puts the pcmcia
scripts
in to load up at bootup, this may cause a bit of a problem.  

I fixed this on my system by appending the following line to the script
that loads
up the i82365.o module:
irq_list=10,13

the pcmcia script is located in /etc/rc.d/init.d/pcmcia

