On Sun, Aug 23, 1998 at 08:45:01PM -0400, Keith Baker wrote:
> I was wrong...  some help would be good...  I think I get the basic
> idea...  but how do I tell it to masq?  when I tell it to go from
> interface to interface that is straight forwarding...  right?  if I tell
> it to go from one ip to the other is that going to setup masqing?

The following two commands are equivalent:

if [ -f /proc/net/ip_fwchains ]; then
  ipchains -A forward -j MASQ -s 192.168.2.0/24 -d 0.0.0.0/0
else
  ipfwadm -F -i accept -S 192.168.2.0/24 -D 0.0.0.0/0 -m
fi


r~


