I did the following: download the generic KDE SRPMS, and
QT 1.33-1rh5 SRPMS from Troll.

I ran this little script (from the directory that contained
the SRPMS and that worked for me...

#!/bin/sh

# On alpha systems QT 1.40 won't run (it WILL build) so use
# QT 1.33 instead.

rpm --rebuild qt-1.33-1rh5.src.rpm
rpm -Uvh /usr/src/redhat/RPMS/alpha/qt*

rpm --rebuild kdesupport-1.0-1.src.rpm
rpm -Uvh /usr/src/redhat/RPMS/alpha/kdesupport*

rpm --rebuild kdelibs-1.0-1.src.rpm
rpm -Uvh /usr/src/redhat/RPMS/alpha/kdelibs*

rpm --rebuild kdebase-1.0-1.src.rpm
rpm -Uvh /usr/src/redhat/RPMS/alpha/kdebase*

rpm --rebuild kdeadmin-1.0-1.src.rpm
rpm --rebuild kdegames-1.0-1.src.rpm
rpm --rebuild kdegraphics-1.0-1.src.rpm
rpm --rebuild kdemultimedia-1.0-1.src.rpm
rpm --rebuild kdenetwork-1.0-1.src.rpm
rpm --rebuild kdestart-1.0-1.src.rpm
rpm --rebuild kdeutils-1.0-1.src.rpm 

rpm -Uvh /usr/src/redhat/RPMS/alpha/kde*

I hope this helps...

Stefan van der Eijk
stefan@stack.nl

PS: kdestart has some runny %Discription
things in the spec file... I edited that
out...


