The 3Com905B-TX was a problem for me as well. I've not used it on alpha 
linux, but for intel linux I had to get the latest  "Vortex" and 
"Boomerang" drivers from  
http://cesdis.gsfc.nasa.gov/linux/drivers/vortex.html. I also had to use it 
as a module and set the following in /etc/config.modules to get it to work 
with my cisco 2924XL 10/100 switch:

alias eth0             3c59x
options 3c59x           options=0x04 

Otherwise it would fail to auto negotiate properly.


