>
>Then the modem reinitializes and redials, in a loop.  Any ideas?  Do
>I have a timeout setting that's incorrect or missing?

I had this problem as well.  It turned out that my modem was disconnecting
because the system was dropping DTR when chat returned control to pppd.  I
solved the problem by flipping a DIP switch on my modem (it's a USR
Sportster 56K) that causes it to ignore DTR.  You may be able to accomplish
the same thing with an AT command in your init string.

-Matt



