Subject: Re: lapack, blas, gemm under linux/axp

A couple of years ago I was working with SPARC systems in France, and I met
a guy (Michel Dayde) who had developed a BLAS-3 library, written in F77,
specifically for RISC architectures.

I tested the library, and found that it significantly outperformed the
CraySoft numerical libraries we had been using up to that point.  The
library is freely available and should perform well for the Alpha
(depending of course on the quality of your compiler), and should fill any
gaps you don't have hand-coded solutions for.  Try looking at:

http://www.enseeiht.fr/fr/Recherche/Info/apo/Blas.html

Regards,
Stig Telfer


