Well, in my case I was bumping into the default limit when I had 120+ shell
scripts (/usr/lib/news/bin/control/newgroup) calling "lockfile" to wait for
their turn to execute.  The 256 processes were essentially sleeping for 30
seconds, looking to see that the given file was owned by another process, and
going to sleep again.

newgroup doesn't normally call lockfile, but when 500 newgroup commands come
in on your newsfeed at once (as was happening this weekend), you can either
deal with load averages in the 100 to 200 range, or you can implement a
locking mechanism like I did.

