On Mon, Aug 31, 1998 at 12:01:06AM -0600, Michal Jaegermann wrote:
> If on Alpha CONFIG_BLK_DEV_IDE is defined then with current kernels
> (2.0.3x) one see the following on a startup:
> 
> kernel: unaligned trap at fffffc00003a3278: fffffc00000061be 28 1
> kernel: unaligned trap at fffffc00003a328c: fffffc00000061c2 28 2
> kernel: unaligned trap at fffffc00003a3278: fffffc00000061ce 28 1
> kernel: unaligned trap at fffffc00003a328c: fffffc00000061d2 28 2
> 
> Here is the corresponding kernel code:
> 
> 0xfffffc00003a3278 <msdos_partition+568>:	ldl	t0,0(t2)
> 0xfffffc00003a327c <msdos_partition+572>:	extbl	t0,0x2,t0
> 0xfffffc00003a3280 <msdos_partition+576>:	and	t0,0x3f,t0
> 0xfffffc00003a3284 <msdos_partition+580>:	cmpeq	t0,0x1,t0
> 0xfffffc00003a3288 <msdos_partition+584>:	
>     beq	t0,0xfffffc00003a32ec <msdos_partition+684>
> 0xfffffc00003a328c <msdos_partition+588>:	ldl	t1,4(t2)
> 0xfffffc00003a3290 <msdos_partition+592>:	extbl	t1,0x2,t0
> 0xfffffc00003a3294 <msdos_partition+596>:	and	t0,0x3f,t0
> 0xfffffc00003a3298 <msdos_partition+600>:	cmpeq	t0,0x3f,t0
> 0xfffffc00003a329c <msdos_partition+604>:	
> 
> It is from linux/drivers/block/genhd.c and traps happen on lines
> marked with '---->':
> 
> 329				for (i = 0; i < 4 ; i++) {
> 330					struct partition *q = &p[i];
> 331					if (NR_SECTS(q)
> 332				----->	   && (q->sector & 63) == 1
> 333				----->	   && (q->end_sector & 63) == 63) {

Linus, the compiler has gotten smart.  It sees that those two character
loads are contained in a structure with known alignment, and optimizes.

I don't see a solution at the moment less gross than just marking the
structure as packed.  Alternately, I suppose we could turn off the 
unaligned access message in the kernel for the 2.2 release.


r~


--- include/linux/genhd.h.orig	Mon Aug 31 12:04:52 1998
+++ include/linux/genhd.h	Mon Aug 31 12:05:09 1998
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ struct partition {
 	unsigned char end_cyl;		/* end cylinder */
 	unsigned int start_sect;	/* starting sector counting from 0 */
 	unsigned int nr_sects;		/* nr of sectors in partition */
-};
+} __attribute__((packed));
 
 struct hd_struct {
 	long start_sect;


